    "status": "transcribed",
    "salutation": "Dear Joan,",
    "body": "Will try and write a few lines tonight if you don't mind, which I think you wouldn't. Hope this finds you in the best of health.\n\nWe got to San Diego sometime Friday afternoon and we really had a nice trip coming out. There were 170 that came out, so we had a special train all the way through. The states we came through were Ill., MO., Kansas, Oklahoma, Texas, New Mexico, Oregon, and California. Everything was nice except the desert. It was around 120 degrees in the shade when we came across and we like to have died.\n\nI am now at the Destroyer Base waiting to be transferred to Honolulu where my ship is at. They don't know when the next ship leaves, but I think in the next few days. There sure will be several miles between me & you when I get out there. You can't tell how long I will be there. Might be 2 years and still it could only be 2 months. I got a funny feeling I'm not going to like the place anyway. California is a nice place to live but still, I will take Old Kentucky. I guess it's because I've lived there all my life.\n\nHave you been down home since I left? You told me you would go more often. Don't know when I'll get another chance to come home. [[It won't be long now before the United States is going to be in the war. If you have seen and heard the things I have you'd think the same way.]]\n\nWhat have you been doing since I left? Working hard, I bet. I am still looking for that picture. Be sure and write me a long letter when you have the time to spare. Joan, send it to the address at the head of the letter; if I'm not here, they will send it on to me.\n\nWith Love,",
    "signature": "Eugene",
